{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And I will give your rains in their season</b> — He placed the matter of the rains first, for when they come in their season as is fitting, the air will be clear and good, and the springs and rivers will be good, and this will be a cause of health for the bodies, and all the fruits will increase and be blessed through them, as He says, \"and the land shall yield its produce and the trees of the field shall yield their fruit.\" And behold, along with this, man will not become ill and there will be among them no miscarrying or barren, and likewise among their animals, and they will fill their days, for when the bodies are large and healthy they will endure like the days of man, and behold, this is the greatest of the blessings. And He said that the heavens will answer the earth with rains in their season, and the earth will answer with its produce, which is vegetation and all living creatures that move — domesticated animal and wild beast and creeping thing and bird, and also the fish, for the earth encompasses the entire lower sphere, as in \"In the beginning Elohim created the heavens and the earth\" (Genesis 1:1), \"And the heavens and the earth were finished\" (ibid. 2:1), and so \"Praise YHWH from the earth, sea-monsters and all deeps\" (Psalms 148:7), and similarly in many places in Scripture. And behold, all the generated beings in the lower realms are the produce of the earth:"], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {0 "Reading בִּהְיוֹת הַגּוּפִים גְּדוֹלִים ('when the bodies are large') as written; the argument appears to be that robust physical constitution enables longevity."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:00:44.106770054Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}